{"step_index":174,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-13T06:21:31Z","input_tokens":5307,"cache_read_tokens":77040,"output_tokens":4567,"thinking":"Initial hypothesis: Network restrictions within the sandbox limit PostgreSQL usage. Considering that, both PostgreSQL and SQLite might be supported; PostgreSQL for standard deployment scenarios and SQLite for local development and testing. Investigating if SQLite integration is possible.\n\n\nInitial investigation indicates that SQLite may be viable for local development and testing, even though PostgreSQL is the intended production database. The `database.py` configuration appears flexible, allowing the application to use a `DATABASE_URL` environment variable, which could point to an SQLite database. Examining the Alembic migration file, SQLAlchemy standard types are used, indicating SQLite compatibility. The focus now shifts to implementing the user's requested business journey.\n\n\nReviewing the core business journey steps: patient registration, referral linking, treatment purchase, reward accrual, commission calculation, and result display. This requires a robust backend encompassing authentication, attribution, sales, points, commissions, and both database and mobile API integrations.\n\n\nAnalyzing the provided schema details, the payment, points, commission, and OTP models are now defined, along with their relationships and data types. These models include key fields such as patient and branch IDs, payment references, commission tiers and ledgers, and OTP-related data. I will ensure all models are exported within the specified initialization file.\n\n\nAnalyzing `auth_service.py` reveals the core authentication and user management logic, including OTP generation/verification, user creation (patient and agent), and JWT token handling. The agent creation process generates unique agent codes and handles referral linking. The referral service provides agent-specific referral information and the ability to pre-register patient leads.\n\n\nThe payment service function now includes referral attribution locking upon patient signup and payment recording logic.  The payment recording function creates a verified payment, converts active referrals, and awards points based on a 1-to-10 ratio of currency spent to points earned. It then calculates and records the agent commission based on the referral and predefined commission tiers, inserting entries into the appropriate ledgers.  Wallet service provides functions to retrieve patient wallet information (points and credit), along with agent earnings including ledger entries.\n\n\nAnalyzing API endpoints for authentication, referrals, payments, and wallet functionalities. Implementation now includes routes for retrieving agent referral codes, creating and linking referrals, simulating treatment purchases, and fetching payment/wallet histories. This data is being integrated within the main application.\n\nThe focus shifts to database configuration, ensuring SQLite support for local environments and graceful PostgreSQL fallback.  A test suite is being designed to validate the complete user journey, encompassing registration, referral linking, treatment purchase, commission calculation, and wallet verification. Now the mobile app screens will be modified to support the implemented user journey.\n\n\nFocusing on the mobile app, the authentication flow now incorporates referral code handling during login and signup, with referral code acceptance in query parameters. The verification screen prompts new users for full name, role, and referral code confirmation.\n\nThe agent's home screen will now display the unique agent code, referral statistics, and buttons for referral simulation. The patient's home screen shows treatment credit balance and a purchase button with referral details.\n\nThe referral tab features the agent's unique link, an \"Add Patient Lead\" form, and referral status displays. The wallet tab presents ledgers for both patients and agents, alongside a treatment purchase simulation.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_file","args":{"Content":"\"import uuid\\n\\nfrom sqlalchemy import (\\n    DateTime,\\n    ForeignKey,\\n    Index,\\n    Integer,\\n    Numeric,\\n    String,\\n    Uuid,\\n    func,\\n)\\nfrom sqlalchemy.orm import Mapped, mapped_column\\n\\nfrom app.base import Base\\n\\n\\nclass Payment(Base):\\n    __tablename__ = \\\"payments\\\"\\n\\n    id: Mapped[uuid.UUID] = mapped_column(\\n        Uuid(as_uuid=True),\\n        primary_key=True,\\n        default=uuid.uuid4,\\n    )\\n\\n    patient_id: Mapped[uuid.UUID] = mapped_column(\\n        Uuid(as_uuid=True),\\n        ForeignKey(\\\"patients.id\\\"),\\n        nullable=False,\\n    )\\n\\n    branch_id: Mapped[uuid.UUID | None] = mapped_column(\\n        Uuid(as_uuid=True),\\n        ForeignKey(\\\"branches.id\\\"),\\n        nullable=True,\\n    )\\n\\n    treatment_name: Mapped[str] = mapped_column(\\n        String(150),\\n        nullable=False,\\n    )\\n\\n    # Stored in cents (e.g. 150000 = R 1500.00)\\n    amount_cents: Mapped[int] = mapped_column(\\n        Integer,\\n        nullable=False,\\n    )\\n\\n    currency: Mapped[str] = mapped_column(\\n        String(10),\\n        nullable=False,\\n        default=\\\"ZAR\\\",\\n    )\\n\\n    # 'pending', 'verified', 'refunded'\\n    status: Mapped[str] = mapped_column(\\n        String(30),\\n        nullable=False,\\n        default=\\\"verified\\\",\\n    )\\n\\n    payment_reference: Mapped[str] = mapped_column(\\n        String(100),\\n        nullable=False,\\n        unique=True,\\n    )\\n\\n    verified_at: Mapped[DateTime | None] = mapped_column(\\n        DateTime(timezone=True),\\n        nullable=True,\\n    )\\n\\n    created_at: Mapped[DateTime] = mapped_column(\\n        DateTime(timezone=True),\\n        nullable=False,\\n        server_default=func.now(),\\n    )\\n\\n    __table_args__ = (\\n        Index(\\\"ix_payments_patient_id\\\", \\\"patient_id\\\"),\\n        Index(\\\"ix_payments_reference\\\", \\\"payment_reference\\\"),\\n    )\\n\"","Path":"\"/Users/ravi/Desktop/Kezza_mobile-main/backend/app/models/payment.py\""}},{"name":"write_file","args":{"Content":"\"import uuid\\n\\nfrom sqlalchemy import (\\n    DateTime,\\n    ForeignKey,\\n    Index,\\n    Integer,\\n    String,\\n    Uuid,\\n    func,\\n)\\nfrom sqlalchemy.orm import Mapped, mapped_column\\n\\nfrom app.base import Base\\n\\n\\nclass PointsLedger(Base):\\n    __tablename__ = \\\"points_ledger\\\"\\n\\n    id: Mapped[uuid.UUID] = mapped_column(\\n        Uuid(as_uuid=True),\\n        primary_key=True,\\n        default=uuid.uuid4,\\n    )\\n\\n    patient_id: Mapped[uuid.UUID] = mapped_column(\\n        Uuid(as_uuid=True),\\n        ForeignKey(\\\"patients.id\\\"),\\n        nullable=False,\\n    )\\n\\n    payment_id: Mapped[uuid.UUID | None] = mapped_column(\\n        Uuid(as_uuid=True),\\n        ForeignKey(\\\"payments.id\\\"),\\n        nullable=True,\\n    )\\n\\n    # Positive for earn, negative for redeem\\n    points: Mapped[int] = mapped_column(\\n        Integer,\\n        nullable=False,\\n    )\\n\\n    balance_after: Mapped[int] = mapped_column(\\n        Integer,\\n        nullable=False,\\n    )\\n\\n    # 'treatment_reward', 'redemption', 'manual_adjustment', 'refund_reversal'\\n    event_type: Mapped[str] = mapped_column(\\n        String(40),\\n        nullable=False,\\n    )\\n\\n    description: Mapped[str] = mapped_column(\\n        String(255),\\n        nullable=False,\\n    )\\n\\n    created_at: Mapped[DateTime] = mapped_column(\\n        DateTime(timezone=True),\\n        nullable=False,\\n        server_default=func.now(),\\n    )\\n\\n    __table_args__ = (\\n        Index(\\\"ix_points_patient_id\\\", \\\"patient_id\\\"),\\n    )\\n\"","Path":"\"/Users/ravi/Desktop/Kezza_mobile-main/backend/app/models/points.py\""}}]}
