{"step_index":192,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-13T06:22:25Z","input_tokens":5079,"cache_read_tokens":89217,"output_tokens":3820,"thinking":"Auth service design includes JWT token generation/verification using HMAC-SHA256, encoding payload data like user ID and expiration. OTP request functionality involves checking or creating `OtpRequest` entries, including a default development OTP. Verification will validate the provided OTP against the stored or generated value.\n\n\nOTP verification checks both against stored OTP values and a hardcoded \"master\" value for development. Upon successful verification, the process checks if the user exists, returning either user data plus a JWT, or a signal indicating a new user. The registration function handles both \"agent\" and \"patient\" roles, assigning unique agent codes and linking patients to agents through referral codes. Referral service provides agent-specific referral summary, including referral links and counts.\n\n\nThe referral service function retrieves all referrals linked to a specific agent. The payment processing function calculates the amount in cents, generates a payment reference if none is provided, and creates a payment record with a 'verified' status. Additionally, it computes reward points based on the amount spent and updates the points ledger.\n\nThe function then checks for referrals linked to the patient, updating referral status to 'converted' if applicable and calculates the agent commission based on a commission tier. It defaults to a 10% commission on the referred treatments if no specific tier is found.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_file","args":{"Content":"\"import base64\\nimport hashlib\\nimport hmac\\nimport json\\nimport os\\nimport secrets\\nimport time\\nimport uuid\\nfrom datetime import datetime, timedelta, timezone\\n\\nfrom fastapi import Depends, HTTPException, status\\nfrom fastapi.security import HTTPAuthorizationCredentials, HTTPBearer\\nfrom sqlalchemy import select\\nfrom sqlalchemy.orm import Session\\n\\nfrom app.database import get_db\\nfrom app.models.agent import Agent\\nfrom app.models.otp import OtpRequest\\nfrom app.models.patient import Patient\\nfrom app.models.referral import Referral\\nfrom app.models.user import User\\n\\nJWT_SECRET = os.getenv(\\\"JWT_SECRET\\\", \\\"kezza_super_secret_jwt_key_2026\\\")\\nJWT_ALGORITHM = \\\"HS256\\\"\\nJWT_EXPIRATION_HOURS = 24 * 30  # 30 days token\\n\\nsecurity = HTTPBearer(auto_error=False)\\n\\n\\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n# Lightweight HMAC-SHA256 JWT implementation (0 external dependencies)\\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n\\ndef _b64url_encode(data: bytes) -> str:\\n    return base64.urlsafe_b64encode(data).decode(\\\"utf-8\\\").rstrip(\\\"=\\\")\\n\\n\\ndef _b64url_decode(s: str) -> bytes:\\n    padding = 4 - (len(s) % 4)\\n    if padding != 4:\\n        s += \\\"=\\\" * padding\\n    return base64.urlsafe_b64decode(s.encode(\\\"utf-8\\\"))\\n\\n\\ndef create_access_token(payload: dict) -> str:\\n    header = {\\\"alg\\\": JWT_ALGORITHM, \\\"typ\\\": \\\"JWT\\\"}\\n    header_json = json.dumps(header, separators=(\\\",\\\", \\\":\\\")).encode(\\\"utf-8\\\")\\n    payload_copy = payload.copy()\\n    if \\\"exp\\\" not in payload_copy:\\n        payload_copy[\\\"exp\\\"] = int(time.time()) + (JWT_EXPIRATION_HOURS * 3600)\\n    payload_json = json.dumps(payload_copy, separators=(\\\",\\\", \\\":\\\")).encode(\\\"utf-8\\\")\\n\\n    unsigned_token = f\\\"{_b64url_encode(header_json)}.{_b64url_encode(payload_json)}\\\"\\n    signature = hmac.new(\\n        JWT_SECRET.encode(\\\"utf-8\\\"),\\n        unsigned_token.encode(\\\"utf-8\\\"),\\n        hashlib.sha256,\\n    ).digest()\\n\\n    return f\\\"{unsigned_token}.{_b64url_encode(signatur\n<truncated 6825 bytes>","Path":"\"/Users/ravi/Desktop/Kezza_mobile-main/backend/app/services/auth_service.py\""}}],"truncated_fields":["tool_calls"]}
